Usage:
  void logs [-f] [-n LINES] <service|file>
  void logs --list

Options:
  -f, --follow           Keep following the log
  -n, --lines N          Number of lines to show (default: 50)
      --list             List known log files and services with logs

Examples:
  void logs NetworkManager
  void logs -f -n 200 sddm
  void logs /var/log/dmesg.log
EOF
}

